er of about C$900M due to award in Q1 2027. VLTX utility order intake was C$670M in Q3 2026.\n  - Data-centre demand is slowing. Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, which is slower than 2026.\n- **Financing (n3):** Utilities can't fund the 2027 plans as filed, so expect some resizing.\n  - Debt is available at a higher cost. Bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp.\n  - Equity is not reliable. Two utility share offerings were cut back in size in Q3.\n  - The risk is that some capex, and so some orders, slip or shrink. The Q1 tender is the key test.\n- **Pricing (n4):** VLTX LEAPS are fairly priced, neither cheap nor expensive. Implied volatility is 27% against a 2-year median of 26%, and the Jan-2029 point is 27.5%. Options give no pricing edge, so the case rests on the fundamentals.\n\n**Suggested approach:** Add a partial tranche now and hold the rest until the Q1 2027 tender award and the next round of utility financing. This is not personalized advice, and I haven't looked at your existing position size or risk limits.","ttft_ms":1982,"type":"result","duration_ms":63448,"uuid":"7eab8aa2-a9f3-44a3-bf81-57efacc5977f","ttft_stream_ms":1056,"time_to_request_ms":96,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":8,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":7,"input_attachments":26,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":11,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":7,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":2,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":61,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":191,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":116,"process_rss_mib_result":198,"process_anon_mib_result":116,"process_peak_rss_mib":199,"process_cpu_ms_t